    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">Android</code></td>
      <td>The Android ecosystem. Android organizes code using <a href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/git-repo/+/HEAD/README.md"><code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">repo</code> tool</a>, which manages multiple git projects under one or more remote git servers, where each project is identified by its name in <a href="https://gerrit.googlesource.com/git-repo/+/HEAD/docs/manifest-format.md#Element-project">repo configuration</a> (e.g. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">platform/frameworks/base</code>). The <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">name</code> field should contain the name of that affected git project/submodule. One exception is when the project contains the Linux kernel source code, in which case <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">name</code> field will be <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:linux_kernel:</code>, followed by an optional SoC vendor name e.g. <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">:linux_kernel:Qualcomm</code>. The list of recognized SoC vendors is listed in the <a href="#android-soc-vendors">Appendix</a></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
